  "概率分布与抽样演示" = "Probability Distributions & Sampling Demos", "统计基础与概率分布" = "Statistics Basics & Probability Distributions",
  "从均值、方差和标准差开始，再认识概率分布、随机抽样、大数定律和中心极限定理。" = "Start with the mean, variance, and standard deviation, then explore probability distributions, random sampling, the law of large numbers, and the central limit theorem.",
  "① 中心位置" = "① Center", "② 离散程度" = "② Spread", "③ 分布形状" = "③ Distribution shape", "④ 抽样规律" = "④ Sampling behavior",
  "基础：均值与方差" = "Basics: Mean & Variance",
  "先回答两个问题：数据集中在哪里？数据有多分散？" = "Start with two questions: where is the center, and how spread out are the data?",
  "均值和中位数描述中心；方差、标准差、四分位距和极差描述离散程度。标准差与原数据单位相同，通常比方差更容易解释。" = "The mean and median describe the center; variance, standard deviation, interquartile range, and range describe spread. Standard deviation uses the original data unit and is usually easier to interpret than variance.",
  "均值" = "Mean", "样本均值" = "Sample mean", "样本方差" = "Sample variance", "标准差" = "Standard deviation", "样本标准差" = "Sample standard deviation", "标准化分数" = "Standard score",
  "把所有观测加总后除以样本量。" = "Add all observations and divide by the sample size.",
  "衡量观测到均值的平方距离；n − 1 是自由度修正。" = "Measures squared distances from the mean; n − 1 is the degrees-of-freedom correction.",
  "标准差与原始数据使用相同单位。" = "Standard deviation uses the same unit as the original data.",
  "表示某个观测距离均值多少个标准差。" = "Shows how many standard deviations an observation is from the mean.",
  "当前分布的理论期望与方差" = "Theoretical Expectation and Variance of the Current Distribution",
  "x̄ = 所有观测之和 ÷ 样本量" = "x̄ = sum of all observations ÷ sample size",
  "s² = 平方离差之和 ÷ (n − 1)" = "s² = sum of squared deviations ÷ (n − 1)",
  "s = √s²，与原始数据单位相同" = "s = √s², in the same unit as the original data",
  "设置分布参数、样本量和重复次数，比较理论结果与随机模拟，并演示大数定律和中心极限定理。" = "Set distribution parameters, sample size, and repetitions to compare theory with simulation and demonstrate the law of large numbers and central limit theorem.",
  "概率分布" = "Probability distribution", "每次样本量" = "Sample size", "重复抽样次数" = "Sampling repetitions",
